# Probe, with load-fire-2 and load-fire-3: an event an 'on load' fires reaches the triggers before it in Skript's
# load order, and not those after it. Skript registers each event's trigger in turn, script by script and line by
# line, and runs each 'on load' when it gets to it. The event is a weather change, which on Folia belongs to the
# global thread 'on load' runs on; only the changes made while {diff::load-fire-on} is set are counted, so the
# weather the world starts with doesn't matter.

on weather change:
	{diff::load-fire-on} is set
	add "1: weather" to {diff::load-fire::*}

function probe_load_fire_1():
	stop
